      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nEncoder-only and pooling models (embeddings, rerankers, classifiers) do not perform autoregressive generation and do not need a KV cache. \r\nPreviously, `CPUWorker.__init__` eagerly required `requested_cpu_memory <= available_memory` at startup, causing models to fail in memory-constrained environments (e.g., container `--memory=5g`) unless users manually passed `VLLM_CPU_KVCACHE_SPACE=0`\r\n\r\nThis PR:\r\n1. Skips the startup memory reservation check in `CPUWorker.__init__` when `runner_type == \"pooling\"`.\r\n2. Automatically sets `kv_cache_size = 0` in `determine_available_memory()` for pooling models, matching GPU worker behavior out-of-the-box.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nRun an encoder-only reranker model without any KV-cache environment variables or flags:\r\n```bash\r\nvllm serve BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3 --dtype bfloat16\r\n```\r\n## Test Result\r\nServer starts cleanly out-of-the-box without requiring VLLM_CPU_KVCACHE_SPACE=0\r\n\r\n\r\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
